<h1><span lang="EN-GB">New Sphere - Non-Interactive</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-US">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Datuming &gt; Non-Interactive &gt;</b> <i style="font-style:normal;">Sphere</i></span>.</i></p>
<p class="description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">New Sphere</span> <span lang="EN-US">command creates new datum sphere .</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify; margin-left:0px;"><img src="Using_Datums_files/image107.gif" width="395px" height="251px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">A new sphere can be created in two ways:</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">by direct input of the centre and the radius;</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">or by selecting existing entity for definition of the sphere centre and direct input of the radius.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Dialog description:</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Name</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Name for the sphere. The default name is ‘Sphere N’, where N is the number of the subsequent newly created datum sphere.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Point</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Select an existing datum point, sphere, or circle from the list to define the centre of the circle or type-in the co-ordinates of the centre manually.</span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Radius</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-US">Radius of the sphere. It must be a positive non-zero value.</span></p>
